title: Orphans in the GUI
tags: [[Orphans]]
kind: reference
summary: An orphaned record's row is purple in the list and its detail says why — deleted or missing — whether or not detection ever ran.

The metarecord list ([[metarecord-list panel]]) paints a row ''purple'' when the record it
shows is orphaned, and [[metarecord-detail panel]] adds a note, both through `panel-shim/orphan.js`: ''deleted'' when
`mfr_path` is `nothing` (the watcher saw the file go), ''missing'' when the stored path no
longer exists on disk (the file vanished while untracked). This is computed on display,
independently of the `orphan` marker detection writes ([[Finding and clearing orphans]]).

Purple is the orphans' colour alone — never the amber of an unplugged volume, whose
records are unavailable rather than gone, and which is checked first
([[Unmounted volumes in the GUI]]).
